  "worked_solution": "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $-1.$ This occurs when $x\\to \\infty .$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\n- The largest $y$-value is $3.$ This occurs when $x\\to -\\infty .$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-1$ and $3,$ not including $-1$ and $3.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-1<y<3,$ which can also be written as $-1<f(x)<3.$",
